-- title:
--   q-expansion of the weight-2m trace Hecke operator
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a field, let $N \ge 1$ with $(N : K) \neq 0$ and let $\ell$ be a prime not dividing $N$ for which $K$ contains a unit $\zeta$ that is a primitive $\ell$-th root of unity. Write $F$ = `modularFunctionFieldC K N` for the $K$-subfield of $K((q))$ generated by $j(q)$ = `jqModC K` and $j(q^N)$ = `jqNModC K N`, and $R$ = `charLDegeneracyRoof K N ℓ` for the $K$-subfield generated by $j(q)$, $j(q^N)$, $j(q^{\ell})$ and $j(q^{N\ell})$; $R$ is viewed as an $F$-algebra along the inclusion `heckeAlphaC`, and `heckeBetaC K N ℓ` denotes the $K$-algebra map $F \to R$ induced by the substitution $q \mapsto q^{\ell}$ on Laurent series. Let $m \ge 1$, let $G \in F$, and let $\varphi \in K[[q]]$ be a power series whose image in $K((q))$ equals $G \cdot (\theta j)^{m}$, where $\theta j$ = `thetaJ K` and `qexpOfWeight K m` is multiplication by $(\theta j)^{m}$. Finally let $h \in R$ satisfy $d(\beta(j)) = h \cdot d j$ in the module of Kähler differentials of $R$ over $K$, where $d j$ is transported from $F$ to $R$ by `KaehlerDifferential.map` and $j$ is the generator `jGeomGen K N`. Then the power series [`ModPForms.heckePS (2m) ℓ φ`](def/CuspForm_ModPForms.html#L20), whose $n$-th coefficient is $a_{n\ell} + \ell^{2m-1} a_{n/\ell}$ (the second term present only when $\ell \mid n$, where $\varphi = \sum_n a_n q^n$), has image in $K((q))$ equal to $(\theta j)^{m}$ times $\ell^{m-1}\,\mathrm{Tr}_{R/F}\!\left(\beta(G)\,h^{m}\right)$, the latter read inside $K((q))$.
--
--   This identifies the classical weight-$2m$ Hecke operator $T_\ell$ on $q$-expansions with the geometric operator $G \mapsto \ell^{m-1}\mathrm{Tr}_{R/F}(\beta(G)h^{m})$ built from the two degeneracy maps of the $\ell$-correspondence and the multiplier $h$ comparing $d(\beta j)$ with $dj$. It is the weight-$2m$ input to the construction of mod-$p$ Hecke eigenforms from eigenvectors in Riemann–Roch spaces, used by the `ModularCurve.SSHeckeV2` results.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_qexpOfWeight_trace_heckeBetaC_mul_pow_eq_heckePS_of_eq_smul_map.lean

